<title>SINGAPORE: Indonesia details September LSWR loading schedule.</title>
<headline>Indonesia details September LSWR loading schedule.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's state oil company, Pertamina has announced the loading schedule for its 3.6 million barrel low sulphur waxy residue (LSWR) allocation for September, traders said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The September allocation was marginally more than August's initial allocation but weak regional demand will put pressure on prices, traders said.</p>
<p>Pertamina's initial allocation of 3.4 million barrels in August was supplemented by 150,000 barrels rolled over from July by the Korean Indonesian Petroleum Company (KIPCO), bringing the volume up to 3.55 million barrels..  </p>
<p>But an additional allocation of 300,000 barrels at the end of July saw a total of 3.845 million barrels lifting from Indonesia in August.</p>
<p>The details of September's loading schedule are as follows (in thousand  barrels):</p>
<p>LOADING FROM FLOATING STORAGE PLATINUM (OFF SUMATRA)</p>
<p>    TIMING	VOLUME	 COMPANY</p>
<p>Sept   1-3	   225	 British Petroleum (BP)</p>
<p>	 1-3	   175	 Indoil</p>
<p>	8-10	   200	 BP</p>
<p>	8-10	   160	 Perta</p>
<p>	8-10	    40	 Far East Investment (FEI)</p>
<p>     16-18	   400	 BP</p>
<p>     25-27	   275	 BP</p>
<p>     25-27	   125	 Indoil</p>
<p>    SUB-TOTAL:   1,600</p>
<p>LOADING FROM PAKNING (SUMATRA)</p>
<p>     10-12	   200	 Pacific Petroleum</p>
<p>    LOADING FROM DUMAI    (SUMATRA)</p>
<p>	 3-5	   100	 Indoil</p>
<p>	 3-5	   100	 Pacific Petroleum</p>
<p>     20-22	   200	 BP</p>
<p>    SUB-TOTAL:     400</p>
<p>LOADING FROM SAMBU JETTY</p>
<p>	 5-7	   200	 Indoil</p>
<p>     18-20	   200	 BP</p>
<p>     28-30	   200	 Indoil</p>
<p>    SUB TOTAL:     600</p>
<p>LOADING FROM BALIKPAPAN (KALIMANTAN, BORNEO)</p>
<p>	 5-7	   120	 Kipco</p>
<p>	 5-7	    80	 Itochu</p>
<p>	9-11	   100	 Itochu</p>
<p>	9-11	   100	 FEI</p>
<p>     20-22	   200	 FEI</p>
<p>     24-26	   200	 FEI</p>
<p>    SUB TOTAL:     800</p>
<p>    TOTAL	  3,600</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
